+
+# Give back single-use coupon on cancel; check free shipping at 50 EUR
+
+Two reports about the order service, each checked against the business rules in `README.md`.
+
+## 1. Welcome code refused after cancelling and re-ordering (Paolo, customer)
+
+Paolo placed an order with his one-time welcome code, cancelled it the same day (wrong size), and the
+corrected order was refused: the code was "already used".
+
+- Rule: "Cancelling it returns its units and gives back its coupon, if the coupon was single-use." A
+  single-use coupon can be used by one order only; if that order is cancelled, it can be used again.
+- Cause: `OrderService.cancel` (`src/orders.ts`) calls `coupons.giveBack(order.coupon, order.customer)`.
+  `Coupons` records the use by order id (`coupons.use(code, id)` in `place`), so giving back by customer
+  name never matches and the code stays used.
+- Fix: give the coupon back for the order's id, `coupons.giveBack(order.coupon, order.id)`.
+
+## 2. Delivery charged on €50.00 of goods (support team)
+
+A customer paid €4.90 delivery on an order whose goods came to exactly €50.00; the site promises free
+delivery from that amount.
+
+- Rule: shipping is free when the goods come to €50.00 or more, after every discount and before VAT.
+- Check: `shippingCost` (`src/shipping.ts`) already tests `goods >= FREE_SHIPPING_FROM_CENTS`, as
+  task-001 made it. Goods of exactly €50.00 after discounts ship free, and a scratch run confirms it.
+- A €4.90 charge therefore means the goods *after discounts* were below €50.00, which the rule allows
+  (for example, a volume discount on a €50.00 gross basket). Without the order's lines and coupon, no
+  code change is justified here. The open question goes back to support for the order details.
+
+## Acceptance
+
+- Report 1: a test that fails before the fix (re-placing the order with the same single-use coupon after
+  cancelling is refused) and passes after it.
+- Report 2: a test pinning the existing behaviour: exactly €50.00 of goods after discounts ships free.
+  No change to `src/shipping.ts`.
+- `npm test` passes in full.
